The three `npm install` invocations never check whether they succeeded. In PowerShell a native command failure only sets `$LASTEXITCODE`; it does not stop the script (and a missing `npm`/Node toolchain raises a non-terminating error that is also ignored). A failed/partial install therefore proceeds silently to the server launch and surfaces as a confusing "module not found" error later. Also, the existence check on `node_modules` treats a stale/partially-installed directory as valid. Validate the toolchain, check `$LASTEXITCODE` after every install, and abort (or at least `exit 1`) on failure ΓÇö e.g.:

```powershell
$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
if (-not (Get-Command npm -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue)) { throw 'npm/Node.js kh├┤ng ─æ╞░ß╗úc t├¼m thß║Ñy. Vui l├▓ng c├ái ─æß║╖t Node.js tr╞░ß╗¢c.' }
function Install-Deps([string]$Prefix, [string]$Label) {
    Write-Host "C├ái ─æß║╖t dependencies $Label..." -ForegroundColor Yellow
    npm install --prefix $Prefix
    if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "npm install cho $Label thß║Ñt bß║íi (exit code $LASTEXITCODE)." }
}
if (-not (Test-Path 'backend\node_modules'))  { Install-Deps 'backend'  'Backend' }
if (-not (Test-Path 'frontend\node_modules')) { Install-Deps 'frontend' 'Frontend' }
if (-not (Test-Path 'node_modules'))          { Install-Deps '.'        'Root' }
```

