content:
The three browser tabs are opened *before* the dev servers are listening (the `concurrently` call that starts them is the last statement), so the tabs almost always show "connection refused" and the user has to reload manually. There is also no way to skip tab opening on a repeat run, so every re-run spawns three more tabs. Consider waiting until the ports accept connections before opening the tabs (e.g. from a background job) and gating the behavior behind a switch:

```powershell
param([switch]$NoBrowser)
function Wait-Port([int]$Port, [int]$TimeoutSeconds = 90) {
    $deadline = (Get-Date).AddSeconds($TimeoutSeconds)
    while ((Get-Date) -lt $deadline) {
        $client = New-Object System.Net.Sockets.TcpClient
        try { $client.Connect('127.0.0.1', $Port); $client.Close(); return $true }
        catch { Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 500 }
    }
    return $false
}
if (-not $NoBrowser) {
    Start-Job -ScriptBlock { if (Wait-Port 3000) { Start-Process 'http://localhost:3000/screen'; Start-Process 'http://localhost:3000/host'; Start-Process 'http://localhost:3000' } }
}
```

`$MyInvocation.MyCommand.Path` is empty when the script is dot-sourced or invoked through `-Command`/a pipeline, so `Split-Path -Parent $null` yields `$null` (or an unexpected path) and `Set-Location` then fails or changes to the wrong directory. In addition, `Set-Location` permanently mutates the caller's working directory when the script is dot-sourced. Use `$PSScriptRoot` with a fallback, validate that the resolved directory really is the project root, and restore the previous location with `Push-Location`/`Pop-Location` in a `try/finally`:

```powershell
$RootPath = if ($PSScriptRoot) { $PSScriptRoot } elseif ($MyInvocation.MyCommand.Path) { Split-Path -Parent $MyInvocation.MyCommand.Path } else { (Get-Location).Path }
if (-not (Test-Path (Join-Path $RootPath 'package.json'))) { Write-Error "Kh├┤ng t├¼m thß║Ñy package.json trong '$RootPath'."; exit 1 }
Push-Location $RootPath
try {
    # ... to├án bß╗Ö phß║ºn kiß╗âm tra dependencies v├á khß╗ƒi chß║íy ...
} finally {
    Pop-Location
}
```

